R-C2 R-AL2 R-AL8 R-AL9 R-DI7 R-H7 R-PH10 R-C1 R-VA6 R-DT2 R-FE1 R-DI1 R-EC10 R-CM4 R-CM7 R-PH12 R-SC1 R-SC8 R-LB4 R-PD9 (slice 011, Q14 of slice 009, Q16 of slice 010, Q26): R-C2 over the full closure in the command code of `update`, and `why`, with the fake Fx, 4 runs on 2 projects (all in one dir with a `.git`).
The header of p1 and p2 is the platform pfx 0.1.1, `mid` 1.0.0 and `core` 1.0.0. `mid` names `text` 1.1.0, and `text` 1.1.0 names `core` 1.1.0 (the chain app, mid, text, core). `text` is no variable of the header, so a check of one level does not see it. The header of `text` 1.1.0 is not in the cache (the fake download makes it). core 1.1.0 is in the cache.
Run 1 (`update --strategy lowest`, p1): the first tuple has core 1.0.0 (the lowest in the range). The calls show that the pick loop fetches `text` 1.1.0 and reads its header before it gives a tuple (R-FE1), and that the index is listed for the 3 free variables only, never for `text` (R-DI1: a transitive group is no variable). The header of `text` names core 1.1.0, so the tuple moves to core 1.1.0 (R-C2 over the full closure): the header changes, and the walk of the closure after the pick has no failure and no new read (the pick holds the headers). Before this slice the pick kept core 1.0.0, and the walk failed with exit 10 (`acme/text 1.1.0 needs acme/core 1.1.0, but the header names acme/core 1.0.0`).
Run 2 (`update`, p2): talon.toml has `core = "acme/core@=1.0.0"`, so core has no release that is 1.1.0 or higher. No tuple: exit 10, the failure of the pick (R-EC10) with the slots in the order of the pick.
Runs 3 and 4 (`why core`, `why text`, p1 after run 1): the paths from the header (Q13: the followed edges). core is direct and reached through mid and text. text is no header entry, a short name finds it (R-SC8). No mark `raised`: the header has core 1.1.0 now.
Slice 016 (R-AL8, R-AL9, R-H7, R-PH10): the pick and the walk have one closure rule, and path entries are nodes of it. Projects p4 and p5 have the platform pfx 0.1.1, `core` 1.0.0 and a path entry `util` (`./util/main.roc`, a package file) that names `core` 1.1.0. Before this slice the pick did not see the edge of a path file (it dropped the path entry): it kept core 1.0.0, and the walk after it failed with exit 10 (`VersionConflict`).
Run 5 (`update --strategy lowest`, p4): the first tuple has core 1.0.0 (the lowest in the range). The pick reads the path file with the headers of its first level (one `read_files` call, no second read in the walk), sees that the file names core 1.1.0, and moves to core 1.1.0 (its header is in the cache). The header changes, exit 0 (R-AL9: a problem of the closure is a conflict of the tuple, the pick tries the next one).
Run 6 (`update`, p5): `talon.toml` has `core = "acme/core@=1.0.0"`, so no variable is free. The pick has no tuple: exit 10, the failure of the pick (R-AL9, R-PH10: exit 10 only when nothing is free), not the failure of the walk after it.
Run 7 (`verify`, p4 after run 5): the pick reads the path file `util` with the headers of its first level, and the walk before the check reads nothing more (the pick holds the file). The tuple passes, nothing is written.
